===Etymology 2===
From the ''lint'' Unix utility, written in 1979, which analyses programs written in the C language<ref>{{quote-web|title=Question “What is linting” on StackOverFlow|url=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8503559/what-is-linting|year=2016|accessdate=February 4, 2016}}</ref>.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To perform a static check on ([[source code]]) to detect stylistic or programmatic errors.
#: {{ux|en|You should '''lint''' your JavaScript code before committing it.}}

